  "reflectionText": "Water came out from under the threshold of the temple, ankle-deep at first, then knee-deep, then to the waist, then a river he could not pass through except by swimming. On each bank stood trees for food, and their leaves for healing. What is it to wade into a river that began as a trickle, and to find the trees on its banks were planted for the healing of the nations?",
